guamp: refused textures logged with their descriptor, and made in a format this GPU holds (Maps: VectorKit received null texture)

fin37d (live-20261103-195840, 479.99 and 502.70 s): Maps aborts with "VectorKit received null texture from Metal". The abort is in
ggl::MetalResourceManager's texture creation (VectorKit 0x1a3760360 in the iPad 17.7.11 cache): newTextureWithDescriptor: (or
newTextureWithDescriptor:iosurface:plane:) returned nil and VectorKit traps. ggl::getPixelFormat asks for A8, R8, R16, R16F, RG8, B5G6R5,
BGR5A1, R32F, RG16, RG16F, RGBA8(_sRGB), BGRA8(_sRGB), RG32F, RGBA16, RGBA16F, RGBA32F, PVRTC (160), ASTC 4x4..12x12 LDR and sRGB,
Depth16/32F, Stencil8, Depth32Float_Stencil8 and YCbCr8_420_2P (500); private storage for depth, stencil and multisample textures,
shared otherwise. Turnip has no VK_IMG_format_pvrtc, and the YCbCr and packed formats depend on the device's answers.
- Every refusal of the device's newTextureWithDescriptor: is logged ("native-metal: texture refused fmt .. type .. usage .. storage ..
  WxHxD mips .. samples .. array ..: why") and sent once per distinct descriptor through the plugin's problem hook ("problem texref a
  f160 t2 u1 s0 256x256 m1 n1"), which patches/native-adreno/0009 prints in the kernel log as "GuampMetal: client Maps: ...".
- Then (NMB_TEXTURE_FALLBACK=0 turns it off): memoryless as private; without shader write, pixel format view and atomic usages; a
  compressed, packed 16-bit or YCbCr format as RGBA8 (sRGB for sRGB) of the same size; Depth32Float_Stencil8 as Depth24Unorm_Stencil8,
  then Depth32Float. A substituted texture reports the asked format, its views use the real one, and its uploads (replaceRegion,
  buffer-to-texture blits) are dropped: it samples clear instead of aborting the app. "native-metal: texture fallback fmt A -> B ...".
Applies after 0001, 0002, 0003, 0009 and 0010; the Objective-C++ is not compiled outside the CI.

